-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Intervene
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Intervene: Gains a second charge and is only usable in Defensive
--           Stance. Generates no rage, and reduces the damage done by the
--           target by 10% for 5 sec."
--
-- Three of the four clauses need no work, and it is worth recording why rather
-- than leaving a future reader to re-derive it:
--
--   "only usable in Defensive Stance" -- already true.  3411 ships with
--       Stances = 131072, which is 1 << (0x12 - 1), FORM_DEFENSIVESTANCE.
--       (Mocking Blow is the one that was wrong; see woa_2026_08_09_01.sql.)
--
--   "Generates no rage" -- already true.  3411 has exactly two effects,
--       SPELL_EFFECT_CHARGE and SPELL_AURA_ADD_CASTER_HIT_TRIGGER.  There is no
--       SPELL_EFFECT_ENERGIZE anywhere in the spell or in 59667, and Improved
--       Charge's +10 rage is masked to Charge only.  Nothing to remove.
--
--   "Gains a second charge" -- NOT IMPLEMENTED, deliberately.  3.3.5a has no
--       spell-charge system: there is no charge category, no recharge timer and
--       nothing in SpellCategory.dbc to hang one on.  Faking it means a hidden
--       marker aura plus RemoveSpellCooldown bookkeeping in C++ (the shape core
--       uses for SPELL_WARRIOR_T10_MELEE_4P_EXTRA_CHARGE, 70849).  That was
--       weighed and dropped rather than smuggled in -- the 30 second cooldown
--       stands.  If it is wanted later, halving the cooldown is the cheap
--       approximation and the marker-aura script is the faithful one.
--
-- So this file implements the fourth clause only.
--
-- "the target" is the party member you Intervene to -- Intervene has no enemy
-- target, so there is no other reading.  The effect is threat management: you
-- jump to whoever pulled aggro, and they ease off for 5 seconds while you take
-- it back.  That pairs with the threat transfer 59667 already does.
--
-- Why a separate spell rather than a third aura effect on Intervene: the
-- debuff has to last 5 seconds and Intervene's own DurationIndex is 1, which is
-- 10 seconds.  An aura applied by Intervene directly would inherit that.
-- 200640 carries DurationIndex 28 (5000 ms) instead.
--
-- 200640 is cloned from 12976 (the Last Stand aura) purely as a chassis: it is
-- the cleanest single-effect aura to hand -- category 0, no attributes, no
-- equipped-item requirement.  Everything meaningful is overridden.  Note
-- EffectImplicitTargetA1 has to move off 1 (TARGET_UNIT_CASTER); left alone the
-- debuff would land on the warrior.  57 is TARGET_UNIT_TARGET_RAID, the same
-- target type Intervene's own effects use (SharedDefines.h:1465).
--
-- Spells:
--   3411   = Intervene
--   200640 = Interceded (new)
-- ============================================================

